  "claim_boundary": "This A0 package freezes only a local, content-addressed request to publish exact SHA-256 commitments for the zero-output source-opportunity contract. Exact ephemeral in-memory derivations used to replay the sealed preflight are not persisted source rows or source materialization. It does not perform a network request, Git commit, push, Gist creation, receipt observation, admission, source materialization, model execution, CUDA execution, or experiment. The current access-controlled origin is explicitly not accepted as public publication. A future public Gist revision may prove only when the same public Gist owner, id, first revision commit, zero-parent history, exact one-entry tree, blob OID, revision-pinned raw URL, filename, and observed request bytes close as one object graph and are anonymously reobserved. That observation is not WORM or trusted time, does not prove producer identity, and cannot rule out pre-anchor seed grinding or machine-global hidden work. Even a valid A0 receipt cannot authorize structural inventory materialization: a separately anchored A1 materializer and single-attempt admission remain mandatory. Appendable, Readable, Learnable, Steerable, and integrated four-axis evidence remain absent."
